e, a high-traffic website. (Traffic) All prior and subsequent edits to the article are noted in its revision history. This article has been viewed enough times in a single year to make it into the Top 50 Report annual list. This happened in 2015, when it received 9,892,611 views. This article has been viewed enough times in a single week to appear in the Top 25 Report 6 times. The weeks in which this happened: December 22 to 28, 2013December 28, 2014 to January 3, 2015January 4 to 10, 2015January 11 to 17, 2015January 18 to 24, 2015January 25 to 31, 2015 Christopher Morcom article[edit]Latest comment: 3 months ago1 comment1 person in discussion Hi I've recently published the Christopher Morcom article and nominated it for good article status. As his relationship with Turing is the reason for his notability, someone interested in Turing might want to review the Morcom good article nomination. Panamitsu ✨ 09:47, 22 April 2026 (UTC)Reply "Alanturing" listed at Redirects for discussion[edit]Latest comment: 2 months ago1 comment1 person in discussion The redirect Alanturing has been listed at redirects for discussion to determine whether its use and function meets the redirect guidelines. Readers of this page are welcome to comment on this redirect at Wikipedia:Redirects for discussion/Log/2026 May 19 § Alanturing until a consensus is reached. 𝔅𝔦𝔰-𝔖𝔢𝔯𝔧𝔢𝔱𝔞? 18:50, 19 May 2026 (UTC)Reply New Ratio Club (and cybernetics) section[edit]Latest comment: 1 month ago1 comment1 person in discussion I've just created a new subsection under Career and Research mainly about his Ratio Club membership but also for any other involvement he had with the post-war cybernetics scene. I don't necessarily want to give the matter that much prominence, but it doesn't seem to fit well into the existing subsections: maybe it could be shoehorned into Early computers and the Turing Test? It also seems too research-related to go under Personal life despite the social aspect. If you have any ideas or